A||N||12||beachbomb||More stinking IDLE problems!!!||||5||
Z||000000||beachbomb||12-11-2000||07:11 PM||||Hi all! My '84 Indy 4 cyclinder still idles at 1900 rpm. I have replaced the following:IAC, TPS, all vacuum hoses, PCV, cleaned trottle body, all temp sensors, even swapped out ECM's,i gave it a major tune up as well. all this and nothing different. What else could it be? I have not replaced the EGR but the insides of it do go up and down. H_E_L_P!!!, thanks..jim(2 '84 Indy's)<BR>p.s. the car does try to drop idle speed sometimes but then goes right back up to 1900!||||reg||5
Z||000001||FIERO1985||12-11-2000||07:26 PM||||check the egr again the egr can have some carbon build up in the system and may only fail at times and that is only 30.00 at your local parts store and also have you pulled your codes and believe me that is a major time and money saving step and go from there <P>good luck<P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||1
Z||000002||beachbomb||12-11-2000||08:44 PM||||Hey fiero1985, i'll check it again, when i checked it before, it had a clogged vaccum line(which i fixed), can i spray cleaner in the egr to help clean it out? I also had pulled the codes off the ECM(was actually my very first step) only codes i had was 12 and 24-of which manual says to discard code 24 if vehicle not moving. If i replace the egr with a new one and if it still doesn't fix it, any ideas after that?..thanks..jim||||reg||7
Z||000003||RedOktober||12-11-2000||09:06 PM||||wow.. sounds like you are having fun (NOT).<P>Have you checked the voltage from your altinator.. I know it doesn't sound related, but if the charging system is not getting the proper voltage, it tells the idle to increase, trying to get more Juice from the altinator.<P>The other problem I've had is the intake manifold becomes carboned up and the gasses going to the EGR aint getting there. Mine was clogged solid.<P>Keep us posted.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Good luck.<P>------------------<BR>86 SE V6 Auto Turbo Going 3.4 OHV "Red Oktober"<BR>86 2M4 5sp (Beater) "Blackie"<BR>87 GT "Blue Flame"||||reg||1
Z||000004||beachbomb||12-12-2000||05:57 AM||||Hey redoktober, those i haven't checked yet, i will though, thanks for the advice, i'll keep you posted, whats the voltage suppose to be on altenator?..thanks..jim||||reg||7
Z||000005||FIERO1985||12-12-2000||03:21 PM||||Spray carb cleaner and that could do the trick for a while but do not spray into the egr tube I had that problem and replaced the EGR and it runs fine Other than that you have eliminated all the other options and The codes that the self method uses are not that detailed or reliable I trust either the SNAP ON scan tool or the OBD II and I believe even a local parts store (autozone, Advance auto parts or pep boys) rents them out but not exactly sure!<P>But good luck any way<BR>Dan<P><P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||1
Z||000006||KnightRyder31||12-12-2000||06:52 PM||||Carb clearner???<BR>Don't you mean fuel injecter cleaner?||||reg||1
Z||000007||KnightRyder31||12-12-2000||06:52 PM||||Carb clearner???!!!<BR>Don't you mean fuel injecter cleaner?||||reg||1
Z||000008||FIERO1985||12-13-2000||05:46 PM||||it does the same , it is in a aerosol can and cleans well but you can also use fuel injector cleaner but really it is just to free some carbon off the EGR. So it really does not matter as long as you get it clean||||reg||1
Z||000009||beachbomb||12-13-2000||07:16 PM||||Well, i replaced my altenator(after Advance auto parts tested my original one and said the diodes were bad), and i still have the high idle problem, no change. only thing i haven't done is replace the EGR valve(which i will do in a couple days), i thought for sure the bad altenator would have fixed it <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> if a new EGR does not fix it, any other ideas, i think i have covered just about everything there is!!, thanks alot..Jim(2 '84 Indys)||||reg||9
Z||000010||Tweek||12-14-2000||09:00 PM||||BEACHBOMB: I would replace the coil. <BR>I bought my first Fiero about a month ago. Up untill last week it has a problem where after it warmed up ('84 by the way) it would stall out, and after 10 minutes of starting it again it would idle at about 2500 rpm (i'm guessing cause the tach don't work). After replacing various other sensors and doulble checking electrical connections and vacuum hoses, and decided to replace the coil. Voila! Now I can drive without worrying about stalling out at a light or anything. Good luck!!||||reg||14
